  "content": {
    "_uid": "a7065fcd-db19-0712-d15c-df2a0eef9f18",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "7cd70e1d-6fec-cfbb-0baa-d5352e49a6b9",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Assistant Professor Dr Suleman Haque, from the Pulmonology section, clarified several common misperceptions on the myths and realities of nicotine withdrawal symptoms. Professor Riaz Qureshi of the Department of Family Medicine, AKU, spoke of the increasingly important role of the family physician in tobacco control measures, while Assistant Professor in the department, Dr Marie Andrades, highlighted important aspects on how to motivate patients to quit smoking. Professor Ehsanullah Syed of the Department of Psychiatry voiced his views on the reasons for the use of tobacco and the psychological aspect of addiction.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Ms Sidra Waheed, final-year student of AKU Medical College, presented a surprising \"Message for Health Professionals\", many of whom are regular smokers in spite of being professionally aware of the consequences. She further articulated the common myth amongst students that smoking relieves stress. The final speaker, Ms Humaira Waheed, from the Department of Nursing Services, AKUH, said that tobacco was a first step to other addictions and portrayed cases from her clinical experiences.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
