    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Tobacco is the world's single largest preventable cause of death,\" said Professor Javaid Ahmed Khan, Head, Section of Pulmonary and Critical Medicine of Aga Khan University, during his talk on \"The Tobacco Epidemic in Pakistan.\" He highlighted the government's misperception regarding the government's \"need and reliance on revenues generated from this industry\" and urged the medical community to \"make our government realise that tobacco control is highly cost-effective as a basic public health package\". Professor Javaid called for urgent official measures to substitute tobacco with alternative crops and support farmers for a specific time period, and further reasoned that governments of the developed countries must take responsibility to pressure transnational companies in preventing them from targeting children and youth in the developing world. Alarming figures were revealed in this context regarding 2002 budgets for tobacco-related education by the Ministry of Health - Rs 2 million as against Rs 61 million for advertising by a tobacco company.",
